comments.body:
Engineering progress: PR #60 implements the two repository-side controls that were still missing here.

Implemented in #60:
- hash-bound public signer lifecycle registry with ACTIVE/RETIRED/REVOKED states;
- explicit rotation semantics and two revocation scopes (`from_time` vs retrospective `all_signatures`);
- signer assessment at historical certificate/signature time;
- custody/recovery declarations that never store private key material;
- practical custody/rotation/revocation runbook;
- exact hash-bound pilot closeout plan/receipt;
- every workspace file must be explicitly RETAIN or DELETE;
- symlink/unsafe-path rejection;
- exact plan-hash confirmation before deletion;
- fail-closed abort if workspace bytes/file set changed after planning;
- post-closeout verification of retained files;
- explicit non-claim that local unlinking proves secure erasure from backups/snapshots/provider systems;
- focused CircleCI `pilot-ops-tests` gate and adversarial tests.

This narrows #9 substantially, but it should remain open. Still genuinely external:
1. counsel-reviewed pilot/SOW/confidentiality/data-handling language;
2. approved business/entity/payment path where needed;
3. exercising the controls in the first true external workflow under #13 and recording any residual founder-only judgment.
